From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 18:39:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] G12 re-audit (seat-48): 52 of the 180 are PROVEN not
 fork-authored - and none of them is unlicensed

HQ ordered the diff-level re-audit. Method: git patch-id --stable on all 180 patch-filename-subject commits against all 3420 non-upstream commits of every third-party remote, plus PR-number resolution against upstream/master.

VERDICT: 46 are BYTE-IDENTICAL to a registered source (36 llama-cpp-turboquant, 10 spiritbuun/buun-llama-cpp); 6 more resolve to merged upstream llama.cpp PRs (#26415 #26841 #25784 #26459 #26307 #26458, each found by git log --grep in upstream/master). 52 proven NOT fork-authored while the ledger called them 'fork-authored, no upstream origin exists'.

AND THE REASSURING HALF, which matters as much: ZERO of the 52 is unlicensed. turboquant, buun and upstream all have retained verbatim notices in licenses/. The exposure is a FALSE CLASSIFICATION CLAIM, not a missing attribution - a distinction the audit was careful not to assume and this pass can now settle.

Each of the 52 carries a per-row reaudit_2026_08_29 verdict naming method, true source and source commit. The rows STAY in the ledger and the ledger stays CLOSED: the exemption is about un-amendable history, not about authorship, and removing them would report 52 more unprovenanced commits without adding one fact. The purpose field no longer claims all 289 are fork-authored - it now says the claim is known false for at least 52 and points at the per-row verdicts. provenance still exits FAIL 27, unchanged.

THE 128 ARE NOT CLOSED, and the limit is stated rather than glossed: patch-id proves sameness, never originality. A port edited on the way in is indistinguishable from original work to it. Sizing for the next pass: ~128 commits of per-commit diff reading against the project each subject names, starting with the 48 whose subjects say port or name TurboQuant/laguna/ROCmFPX.

PUBLISH-DISCLOSURE-DRAFT.md section 2 rewritten from 'not claimed' to the verdict table. Still a draft, still unpublished.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native)
